  "title": "Quantum-computing universe (Zizzi)",
  "role": "model",
  "summary": "Paola Zizzi: space-time at the Planck scale is discrete and qubitized, each Planck pixel of area holding one qubit, so quantum space-time is a quantum computer. The inflationary universe is a growing quantum register that self-reduces at the end of inflation by objective reduction, conjectured to be a conscious event like a human one. The mind has quantum, classical and non-algorithmic modes.",
